{"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/OmniLight3D","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/omnilight3d"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot11OmniLight3DC","symbolKind":"class","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OmniLight3D","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OmniLight3D","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Class","title":"OmniLight3D"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"OmniLight3D","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An Omnidirectional light is a type of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Light3D","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" that emits light in all directions. The light is attenuated by distance and this attenuation can be configured by changing its energy, radius, and attenuation parameters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When using the Mobile rendering method, only 8 omni lights can be displayed on each mesh resource. Attempting to display more than 8 omni lights on a single mesh resource will result in omni lights flickering in and out as the camera moves. When using the Compatibility rendering method, only 8 omni lights can be displayed on each mesh resource by default, but this can be increased by adjusting ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProjectSettings\/rendering\/limits\/opengl\/maxLightsPerObject"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Note"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When using the Mobile or Compatibility rendering methods, omni lights will only correctly affect meshes whose visibility AABB intersects with the light’s AABB. If using a shader to deform the mesh in a way that makes it go outside its AABB, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GeometryInstance3D\/extraCullMargin"},{"text":" must be increased on the mesh. Otherwise, the light may not be visible on the mesh.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Omnidirectional light, such as a light bulb or a candle."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Light3D"],"title":"Inherits From","kind":"relationships","type":"inheritsFrom"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SQ","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SH","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s12IdentifiableP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VariantConvertible"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/OmniLight3D\/omniAttenuation","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/OmniLight3D\/omniRange","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/OmniLight3D\/omniShadowMode"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/OmniLight3D\/godotClassName"]},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/OmniLight3D\/ShadowMode"],"title":"Enumerations","generated":true,"anchor":"Enumerations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/OmniLight3D/omniShad